description: Registry source for SQLite-backed ToolForge template persistence
includes:
  - crates/sigil-registry/src/
excludes:
  - crates/sigil-registry/target/
context: |
  This scope is the implementation-level view of the registry crate.
  Keep it focused on persistence, record shaping, and query ergonomics for tool
  templates.

  The current source owns:
  - `TemplateRecord`, the in-memory representation of a stored tool template
  - `TemplateStore`, the SQLite-backed access layer
  - schema creation plus add/get/search/list/update/count helpers
  - default template seeding for an empty registry

  Avoid moving compiler validation or runtime execution into this crate; those
  responsibilities stay in `sigil-compiler` and `sigil-runtime`.
related:
  - crates/sigil-registry/.scope
  - crates/sigil-cli/.scope
tags:
  - registry
  - src
  - sqlite
  - toolforge
